error[E0277]: a handler of the form `BatchOut` is not available on the embassy runtime
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_local_batch_out.rs:24:47
   |
24 |     EmbeddedApp::new().with_broker(bus, |b| b.include(bill).out(Audit, LocalMemoryPublish))
   |                                               ^^^^^^^ this handler takes `Out` slots in a form the embassy runtime does not mount
   |
   = help: the trait `ruststream_runtime::router::form_out::SlotsOn<BatchOut>` is not implemented for `LocalPipeline`
   = note: on the embassy runtime a batch handler takes no `Out` parameter (publish from a handler that takes one message at a time), and a handler with an `Out` parameter does not reply (publish the reply through a slot of its own)
help: the following other types implement trait `ruststream_runtime::router::form_out::SlotsOn<Form>`
  --> $WORKSPACE/crates/ruststream-runtime/src/router/form_out.rs
   |
   |           impl SlotsOn<$form> for PublishIdentity {}
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `PublishIdentity`
   |
   |           impl<Head: PublishLayer, Tail: PublishPipeline> SlotsOn<$form> for PublishStack<Head, Tail> {}
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `PublishStack<Head, Tail>`
...
   | / slot_form! {
   | |     forms::Out => InjectMount, NoReply, RouterOut,
   | |     forms::BatchOut => BatchInjectMount, NoReply, RouterOut,
   | |     forms::PublishingOut => PublishInjectMount, DefaultReply, RouterPublishingOut,
   | |     forms::RawReplyOut => RawReplyInjectMount, DefaultReply, RouterPublishingOut,
   | |     forms::BatchPublishingOut => BatchPublishInjectMount, DefaultReply, RouterPublishingOut,
   | | }
   | |_- in this macro invocation
   = note: required for `BatchOut` to implement `ruststream::runtime::RouterMount<Router<ruststream::memory::local::LocalMemoryBroker<4>, (), (), Identity, LocalPipeline>, SubscriberBuilder<FnBody<bill, for<'a, '__rs, 'b, 'c, 'd> fn(BodyTag<bill>, &'a [Reading<'__rs>], &'b Outs<(_,)>, &'c mut ruststream::prelude::Context<'d, (), _>) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Vec<HandlerOutcome>>> {bill::<_, _>}>, LocalMemorySource, (Open, Open, Open, Open)>>`
   = note: this error originates in the macro `slot_form` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

error[E0277]: this batch subscriber has no batch size
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_local_batch_out.rs:24:24
   |
24 |     EmbeddedApp::new().with_broker(bus, |b| b.include(bill).out(Audit, LocalMemoryPublish))
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^ a batch handler needs one
   |
   = help: the trait `BatchSized` is not implemented for `SubscriberBuilder<Sealed<HandleValue<BatchDeserialized<Reading<'static>>, (), Outs<(Slot<Audit, LocalMemoryPublisher<4>, JsonCodec, LocalPipeline>,)>, (), FnBody<bill, for<'a, '__rs, 'b, 'c, 'd> fn(BodyTag<bill>, &'a [Reading<'__rs>], &'b Outs<(_,)>, &'c mut ruststream::prelude::Context<'d, (), _>) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Vec<HandlerOutcome>>> {bill::<_, _>}>, ruststream::runtime::Probed>>, LocalMemorySource, (Open, Open, Open, Open)>`
   = note: add `.batch(nonzero!(n))` at the mount site: the batch size is the one parameter the framework passes to the broker, and the broker's own batching options (a block timeout, a consumer group) ride its subscription source
